<h2>1. Parties</h2>
<p>
  These terms are between you and {operatorName} ({operatorBusinessId}, {operatorAddress}), which provides the AI-Notepad
  subscription service. By creating an account or using the service you accept these terms and the
  <a href={pagePath("privacy", "en")}>Privacy policy</a>.
</p>

<h2>2. The service</h2>
<p>
  AI-Notepad is a Mac app that transcribes, translates and takes notes of meetings. In the subscription edition,
  transcription and AI processing run through our server with our provider accounts. The app's source code is open under
  the Apache 2.0 licence; these terms govern the hosted service, not the code.
</p>

<h2>3. Your account</h2>
<ul>
  <li>You create your account with Sign in with Apple or an email link. You must be 18 or older to use the service.</li>
  <li>Your account is personal; you are responsible for protecting your sign-in and your devices.</li>
  <li>Creating several accounts to multiply the free trial is not allowed.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Free trial</h2>
<p>
  Every new account starts with 3 free meetings; trial meetings can be up to 90 minutes long. To prevent abuse, the trial
  is also limited per device and network.
</p>

<h2>5. Subscription and payment</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The subscription costs USD 5.99 a month. The price excludes VAT; taxes are calculated at checkout based on your location and shown before you pay.</li>
  <li>Payments are handled by Stripe. The subscription renews automatically every month until cancelled.</li>
  <li>If a payment fails, Stripe retries for a few days; you keep access for up to 7 days after the period ends, after which new meetings can't be started.</li>
  <li>If we change the price, we tell you at least 30 days in advance; the change applies from the next period and you can cancel.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Cancelling and withdrawal</h2>
<p>
  You can cancel at any time from your account page through Stripe's portal; you keep access until the end of the paid
  period. Consumers in the EU may withdraw within 14 days of first subscribing. Because you asked for the service to start
  immediately, a withdrawal refunds the amount paid minus the value of the service provided until then. Otherwise we don't
  refund partial periods; your mandatory consumer rights are unaffected.
</p>

<h2>7. Fair use</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The subscription covers up to 10 hours of meetings a month; the limit resets on the first day of each month (UTC).</li>
  <li>A single meeting can last up to 4 hours. Up to 20 meetings can be started per day, and AI usage has daily and monthly ceilings.</li>
  <li>At a limit, the app tells you clearly and new meetings can't be started; your existing notes stay available.</li>
  <li>To protect overall cost, the service may pause temporarily (for example when a daily spending ceiling is reached).</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Before recording, you are responsible for informing participants and obtaining any consent required by applicable law.</li>
  <li>You may not use the service for unlawful purposes, to infringe others' rights, or to record conversations you are not entitled to record.</li>
  <li>Accessing the server outside the app, trying to circumvent limits or device attestation, reselling the service or overloading it is not allowed.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Your content and AI output</h2>
<p>
  Your meeting content and notes belong to you. You allow us to process them only as needed to provide the service; we
  don't store your content or use it for model training. Transcripts, translations and notes are produced by AI and can be
  wrong or incomplete; verify them before important decisions.
</p>

<h2>10. Third-party services</h2>
<p>
  You connect integrations such as Notion, Slack, Linear and Jira with your own accounts; those services have their own
  terms and we are not responsible for how they work.
</p>

<h2>11. Availability</h2>
<p>
  We take care to keep the service running, but we don't commit to a specific uptime. The service may pause for
  maintenance, third-party outages or security reasons. We may improve or change features; we announce in advance any
  change that narrows the core scope of the subscription.
</p>

<h2>12. Liability</h2>
<p>
  To the extent permitted by law, our liability is limited to the total you paid us in the 12 months before the event and
  excludes indirect damages. This limit does not apply to intent or gross negligence, or to mandatory consumer rights.
</p>

<h2>13. Termination</h2>
<p>
  You can delete your account at any time on the <a href={pagePath("account", "en")}>account page</a>. If you seriously or
  repeatedly breach these terms, we may suspend or close your account; where possible we write to you first.
</p>

<h2>14. Changes</h2>
<p>
  If we change these terms, we announce material changes in the app or by email at least 30 days before they take effect.
  If you don't agree, you can cancel your subscription.
</p>

<h2>15. Governing law</h2>
<p>
  Finnish law governs these terms. If you are a consumer, the mandatory consumer protection rules of your country of
  residence still apply, and you can take a dispute to the Finnish Consumer Disputes Board (Kuluttajariitalautakunta) or the
  competent authorities in your country.
</p>

<h2>16. Contact</h2>
<p>{contactEmail}</p>
